# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, R-11). L §2.4: a one-line def with notes "means the long form, the same def with its one
# rule labelled base and those notes": `replace rule rate.base` in a later version replaces that rule (L §5.11), so
# q2, at the cut that sees v2, reads r2 = 0.07; q, as known before v2, reads r = 0.05.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input r: num
input r2: num
def rate: num = r at reader
  note "the rate the bank states"
ask q: rate law 2026-06-30 as known 2025-12-15
ask q2: rate law 2026-06-30

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  r = 0.05
  r2 = 0.07

version v2
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  replace rule rate.base = r2
=== expect
q: 0.05
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2025-12-15
q2: 0.07
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
